o was poised to make an impact before suffering an injury in the summer, is no longer on the team.","published":"2026-11-18T19:16:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50523034/alabama-running-back-prospect-ak-dear-no-longer-team","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Judge questions LSU's claims the SEC 'hallucinated' citations","description":"At a hearing Wednesday in the SEC's lawsuit against LSU, a federal judge pushed back on LSU attorneys for using the word \"hallucinated\" in filing.","published":"2026-11-18T22:40:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522883/judge-questions-lsu-claims-sec-hallucinated-citations","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 College Football Playoff National Championship odds","description":"Odds and futures to win the 2027 College Football Playoff National Championship.","published":"2026-11-18T22:17:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/47664633/2027-college-football-playoff-national-championship-odds-futures","type":"Story","byline":"Doug Greenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Urban Meyer not a candidate for open Maryland job","description":"Urban Meyer has not spoken to Maryland in any formal capacity about its vacant head coaching position and is not a candidate for the job, sources told ESPN's Pete Thamel on Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-18T18:30:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522632/sources-urban-meyer-not-candidate-open-maryland-job","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Davenport RB Cephus Harris III to enter transfer portal","description":"Davenport's Cephus Harris III, the leading rusher in Division II and a candidate for the Harlon Hill Trophy, plans to enter the transfer portal, he told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-18T17:52:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522473/davenport-rb-cephus-harris-iii-enter-transfer-portal","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4899488/amauri-washington","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A%27Mauri_Washington"},"pick":{"pick":29,"round":1,"team":"MIN","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"A'Mauri Washington","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A%27Mauri_Washington","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-18T13:13:47Z","intro":"A'Mauri Washington is an American college football defensive tackle for the Oregon Ducks.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Washington attended Oak Park High School in Oak Park, Michigan for his freshman and sophomore years before transferring to Chandler High School in Chandler, Arizona for his junior and senior years. He committed to the University of Oregon to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Washington was a backup his first two years at Oregon in 2023 and 2024, appearing in 22 games and recording 12 tackles. He became a starter for the first time his junior year in 2025."}]}}